course: dictionary
lesson: 7039
title: Context clues with a bird
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A list around a word can be a clue. «The stew is made of partridges, pheasants, chickens, hares, rabbits, pea-hens, guinea-fowls and one or two other things.» Every item in that list is a bird or animal that people cook, so a partridge must be one of them.
explain: Test your guess by swapping it into the sentence. «The stew is made of a plump brown bird that lives in fields» still makes sense, so the guess fits. Good readers always check this way.
explain: Some words appear in more than one place with different uses. In the carol «The Twelve Days of Christmas», there is «a partridge in a pear tree». In science, a partridge is a game bird. The words around the word tell you which meaning you need.
fact: A partridge is a plump brown bird that lives on the ground in fields.
fact: Partridges are sometimes hunted for food.
fact: In the carol «The Twelve Days of Christmas», there is «a partridge in a pear tree».
fact: In science, a partridge is called a game bird.
fact: Context clues, such as a list of foods, can help you work out what an unknown word means.
exercise: «The stew is made of partridges, pheasants, chickens, hares and rabbits.» What kind of thing is a partridge in this sentence? | A song sung at Christmas | A tree that grows pears | A type of cloud | *A bird or animal used as food
exercise: Which of these is a partridge? | A fish that swims in the sea | A sweet pudding | *A game bird that lives on the ground in fields | A small hairy animal that digs holes
exercise: The dictionary says a partridge is «sometimes hunted for food». What does hunted mean here? | Painted in bright colours | *Chased and caught for food | Sung in a carol | Cooked in a pot
test: In science, what is a partridge called? | A pear | *A game bird | A carol | A stew
test: What does plump suggest about a partridge? | Very fast | Thin and tall | *Round and fat | Bright blue
exam: Ella meets the word partridge in a carol. What is the best first step? | Skip the whole carol and never come back to it | *Read the words around it for clues, then test your guess in the sentence | Ignore the word and hope it does not matter | Guess it is a pear because of the pear tree
